{"title":"Career Roadmap · Nano-Fabrication Engineer","role":"Nano-Fabrication Engineer","summary":"A Nano-Fabrication Engineer works on the fabrication, processing, characterization and integration of micro- and nanoscale devices and structures. The role sits at the intersection of semiconductor processing, materials science, electronics, physics, chemistry and manufacturing engineering.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Micro & Nano Electronics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Nano-Fabrication Engineer works on the fabrication, processing, characterization and integration of micro- and nanoscale devices and structures. The role sits at the intersection of semiconductor processing, materials science, electronics, physics, chemistry and manufacturing engineering."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Semiconductor fabrication"},{"text":"MEMS/NEMS"},{"text":"Nanoelectronics"},{"text":"CMOS processing"},{"text":"Thin films"},{"text":"Lithography"},{"text":"Etching"},{"text":"Deposition"},{"text":"Wafer processing"},{"text":"Nanomaterials"},{"text":"Sensors"},{"text":"Photonics"},{"text":"Advanced packaging"},{"text":"Process integration"},{"text":"Device characterization"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A nano-fabrication engineer is not simply a \"nanotechnology researcher.\" The strongest candidates understand the complete process flow from wafer preparation to fabricated device and characterization."},{"type":"flow","items":["Wafer","Cleaning","Oxidation / Deposition","Photoresist","Lithography","Etching","Doping / Implantation","Metallization","Patterning","Packaging","Electrical / Material Characterization"]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Semiconductor Processing","Nanofabrication","Lithography","Thin Film